  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Quiet Switchboard",
    "overview": "RaktSetu plays the voice-assistant category standard straight: a near-black room, one living orb at its centre, and a precise live-status board beside it. The orb is the only object allowed to glow; everything else is flat, hairline-seamed, and set in the system sans at small, exact sizes. The screen exists to prove what the voice said, so the board reads like an instrument panel rather than a page.\n\nColour carries meaning, never mood. Five state hues (green, blue, amber, red, violet) appear only where a call, gate or line is in that state, almost always as a tinted wash with matching text. The deadline and the confirmed-unit count are the loudest typography on screen; nothing decorative competes with them.\n\nDensity is operator-grade: 12 to 14.5px text, 34px controls, tabular figures for every count and time. Motion is restrained and state-driven (a dialing ring, a confirmation flash, the orb's audio-driven deformation), and all of it collapses under reduced motion.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Near-black ground with two lifted surface steps and hairline seams; no shadows.",
      "One signature: the periwinkle-to-indigo orb that deforms from live audio.",
      "State colour only for meaning, as 12-14% tinted washes with full-strength text.",
      "System UI sans throughout; tabular numerals on every figure.",
      "Pills for status, small radii for controls, full circles for voice controls."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Meaning-Only Rule",
        "body": "A state hue appears only where something is in that state. No hue is used for emphasis, decoration, or brand.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Wash-Not-Fill Rule",
        "body": "State is shown as a tinted wash with full-strength text of the same hue. Solid state fills are reserved for LIVE and end-call, the two moments that touch the real world.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Voice Owns Periwinkle Rule",
        "body": "Periwinkle marks the voice and keyboard focus. It is never a button fill.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Rule",
        "body": "Every count, unit, time and countdown uses tabular figures.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Weight-Ladder Rule",
        "body": "Hierarchy moves through weights 450, 550, 600, 650 at small size steps; do not introduce a display face or sizes above the 40px figure.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Seam Rule",
        "body": "Regions are divided by 1px seams, never by gaps of colour or cards floating on ground.",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Glow Rule",
        "body": "Only the orb emits light. No box-shadows on panels, cards, buttons or popovers.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
